      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Database access is persistently denied (server-side auth error across 5 attempts), so verification via `mysql_query` is impossible; the SQL is constructed strictly from semantic-network definitions, the provided hints, and gold-metric precedents (dw_1888, dw_505, dw_126, dw_3280 running-sum pattern).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables**\n- **FCLT_BUILDING** — current building inventory, one row per building. Key columns: `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY` (building number, e.g. '32'), `BUILDING_NAME`, `BUILDING_TYPE` ('ACADEMIC'/'SERVICE'/'RESIDENT'), `OWNERSHIP_TYPE` ('OWNED'/'LEASED'), `SITE` ('MIT', 'BATES', …), `CAMPUS_SECTOR` ('MAIN GROUP', 'EAST', …), `EXT_GROSS_AREA` (extended gross area, m²), `ASSIGNABLE_AREA`, `NUM_OF_ROOMS`.\n- **FCLT_BUILDING_HIST** — one row per building per fiscal period (201505–201906, 48 periods). Key columns: `FISCAL_PERIOD` (YYYYMM snapshot stamp), `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY`, `ASSIGNABLE_AREA` (per-period assignable area, m²), `BUILDING_NAME`, plus per-period copies of type/site/sector.\n- **FCLT_ROOMS** — one row per physical room. Key columns: `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY` (joins to building), `AREA` (room area in m²), `MAJOR_USE_DESC` (major use description; the FCLT_MAJOR_USE lookup documents codes 'RESIDENT' residential, 'LABS' laboratories).\n- **FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1** — identical to FCLT_BUILDING_HIST except DD-MON-YY date formatting; not needed (no date columns requested).\n- **FCLT_ROOMS_HIST** — room history, but covers only period 201505; the question's room-area filter maps to FCLT_ROOMS per the hint.\n- **FCLT_MAJOR_USE / FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST** — major-use lookup (code/description/assignable). Not needed: `MAJOR_USE_DESC` is denormalized on FCLT_ROOMS and the hint anchors the filter there.\n- **FAC_BUILDING / FAC_ROOMS** — FAC_* family mirrors keyed by FAC_BUILDING_KEY/FAC_ROOM_KEY; wrong key family for FCLT_BUILDING_HIST joins.\n- **BUILDINGS** — space-domain lightweight lookup; square feet, no type/ownership/site/sector classification → cannot support the filters.\n\n**Metrics (precedents)**: dw_1888 (academic + MIT + Stata exclusion via `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> 32`; FCLT_BUILDING↔FCLT_BUILDING_HIST↔FCLT_ROOMS joins), dw_505 (`b.BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC' AND b.SITE='MIT'` on FCLT_BUILDING joined to hist), dw_126 (window over hist rows), dw_488/dw_1190 (room AREA stats joined via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY), dw_76 (Stata = key '32'), dw_1357/dw_12/dw_2596 (hist-based building stats).\n\n**Concepts**: concept_building_inventory (decision guide: current filters → FCLT_BUILDING; per-fiscal-period values → FCLT_BUILDING_HIST), concept_room_space_inventory (room area in m² → FCLT_ROOMS), concept_room_major_use_classification (MAJOR_USE codes RESIDENT/LABS).\n\n**Column concepts**: column_concept_building_type_site (current-snapshot filters on FCLT_BUILDING for \"academic building at MIT\"), column_concept_assignable_area (per-fiscal-period assignable area → FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.ASSIGNABLE_AREA), column_concept_fiscal_period (history snapshot stamp), column_concept_num_of_rooms (not required by this question).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- FCLT_BUILDING ↔ FCLT_BUILDING_HIST via `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY` (1 : ~48 periods); FCLT_BUILDING_HIST ↔ FCLT_ROOMS via `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY` (documented in the hint's Join Keys and used in dw_488, dw_1190, dw_1888).\n- All three gold tables belong to `concept_building_inventory` / `concept_room_space_inventory`; precedent metrics dw_505, dw_126, dw_1888, dw_1190 all consume the FCLT_BUILDING + FCLT_BUILDING_HIST (+ FCLT_ROOMS) combination for exactly this question shape.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix**\n\n| Dimension | FCLT_BUILDING | FCLT_BUILDING_HIST | FCLT_ROOMS | FAC_*/BUILDINGS alternatives |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | 1 row/building (desc) | 1 row/building/period (desc) | 1 row/room (desc) | FAC: same shapes, different key family; BUILDINGS: no classification attrs (concept_building_inventory) |\n| FISCAL_PERIOD | absent (columns) | present (columns) | absent (columns) | only *_HIST tables carry it |\n| ASSIGNABLE_AREA per period | current only | per period (column_concept_assignable_area) | n/a | BUILDINGS in sq ft (units caveat) |\n| BUILDING_TYPE/OWNERSHIP_TYPE/SITE/CAMPUS_SECTOR/EXT_GROSS_AREA | all present | present but per-period | n/a | BUILDINGS lacks all (concept comparison) |\n| AREA / MAJOR_USE_DESC | n/a | n/a | present, m² | ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD has no area (concept_room_space_inventory) |\n| Fan-out risk | none (1:1) | ×48 periods per building | ×rooms per building | FAC keys don't join FCLT hist |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness**\n- Measure `SUM(room AREA)` with MAJOR_USE_DESC filter → FCLT_ROOMS: **SUPPORTED** (AREA, MAJOR_USE_DESC columns exist); FAC_ROOMS: supported structurally but **VIOLATES** join-key family with FCLT_BUILDING_HIST; ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD: **NOT-SUPPORTED** (no area).\n- `FISCAL_PERIOD` output → FCLT_BUILDING_HIST: **SUPPORTED**; FCLT_BUILDING/FCLT_ROOMS: **NOT-SUPPORTED** (column absent).\n- Running sum of `ASSIGNABLE_AREA` per period → FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.ASSIGNABLE_AREA: **SUPPORTED** (decision_guide: \"statistics across a building's history records → FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.ASSIGNABLE_AREA\").\n- Partition key `CAMPUS_SECTOR`, filters `BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC'`, `OWNERSHIP_TYPE='OWNED'`, `SITE='MIT'`, output `BUILDING_NAME`, `EXT_GROSS_AREA`, Stata exclusion `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY<>'32'` → FCLT_BUILDING: **SUPPORTED** (all columns documented; hint anchors all of them to FCLT_BUILDING).\n- FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1: **SUPPORTED** but redundant (identical except date format; no dates requested) — decision guide says use FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.\n- FCLT_ROOMS_HIST: **NOT-SUPPORTED** for a multi-period room measure (covers only 201505) and not in the gold-table list.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**\n- \"academic building … owned by MIT\" → hint maps to FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC', OWNERSHIP_TYPE='OWNED', SITE='MIT' (current-snapshot semantics per column_concept_building_type_site decision guide: \"Questions about current academic … buildings at a site → prefer FCLT_BUILDING\").\n- \"rooms used for 'RESIDENT' or 'LABS' purposes\" → FCLT_ROOMS.MAJOR_USE_DESC IN ('RESIDENT','LABS') (hint; FCLT_MAJOR_USE documents these exact codes).\n- \"fiscal period\" → FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FISCAL_PERIOD (hint).\n- \"running sum of assignable area within each campus sector\" → SUM(FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.ASSIGNABLE_AREA) OVER (PARTITION BY FCLT_BUILDING.CAMPUS_SECTOR ORDER BY FISCAL_PERIOD, BUILDING_NAME) (hint columns; dw_3280 precedent for \"running sum within each X ordered by Y\" = windowed SUM).\n- \"external gross area\" → FCLT_BUILDING.EXT_GROSS_AREA (\"Extended gross area … in square meters\", hint).\n- \"not the Stata building\" → FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> '32' (hint; dw_1888 precedent `b.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> 32`, dw_76 confirms Stata = key '32').\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence**\n- FCLT_BUILDING+FCLT_BUILDING_HIST join on FCLT_BUILDING_KEY: dw_505, dw_126, dw_1888, dw_12 (4 precedents); on COST_CENTER/COLLECTOR keys: dw_1190, dw_2596 (2, used only for history-record counting — not this task's shape).\n- FCLT_ROOMS joined via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY for AREA stats: dw_488, dw_1190, dw_1888, dw_1357 (4 precedents).\n- Stata exclusion via key 32: dw_1888 (1 precedent).\n- FAC_*/BUILDINGS in same-shape metrics: 0 precedents.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nFCLT_BUILDING serves current classification filters and building-level measures; FCLT_BUILDING_HIST serves fiscal-period trend/window analytics (dw_505 stddev, dw_126 windowed MIN, dw_12 rollups); FCLT_ROOMS serves room-area and use-classification statistics (dw_488, dw_1888). The three-table combination is the standard \"Facility Space Analysis\" pattern in this warehouse.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- FCLT_BUILDING, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS, FCLT_MAJOR_USE — semantic_get ✓; FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST, FAC_BUILDING, FAC_ROOMS, BUILDINGS — semantic_get ✓.\n- Metrics dw_1888, dw_505, dw_488, dw_1190, dw_126, dw_76, dw_1357, dw_12, dw_2596 — semantic_get ✓ (full SQL).\n- Concepts concept_building_inventory, concept_room_space_inventory, concept_room_major_use_classification — semantic_get ✓.\n- Column concepts column_concept_building_type_site, column_concept_assignable_area, column_concept_fiscal_period, column_concept_num_of_rooms — semantic_get ✓.\n- mysql_query: attempted 5× — all failed with server-side \"Access denied\" (noted explicitly; verification impossible).\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** FCLT_BUILDING (filters BUILDING_TYPE/OWNERSHIP_TYPE/SITE, Stata exclusion, partition key CAMPUS_SECTOR, outputs BUILDING_NAME & EXT_GROSS_AREA) + FCLT_BUILDING_HIST (FISCAL_PERIOD, per-period ASSIGNABLE_AREA for the running sum) + FCLT_ROOMS (AREA, MAJOR_USE_DESC filter).\n\n**6b.** Join b→h→r on FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; filter `BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC' AND OWNERSHIP_TYPE='OWNED' AND SITE='MIT' AND MAJOR_USE_DESC IN ('RESIDENT','LABS') AND FCLT_BUILDING_KEY<>'32'`; aggregate per (building, fiscal period) with `HAVING SUM(r.AREA) > 1000`; compute the running sum in an outer query as `SUM(ASSIGNABLE_AREA) OVER (PARTITION BY CAMPUS_SECTOR ORDER BY FISCAL_PERIOD, BUILDING_NAME)` so it applies to the filtered rows; final ORDER BY FISCAL_PERIOD, BUILDING_NAME. No rounding. Caveat: h.ASSIGNABLE_AREA is included in GROUP BY (functionally dependent on building+period, prevents aggregation errors); the b↔h join fans out ×48 periods, which is intended since fiscal period is an output dimension.\n\n**6c.** Data: all required columns physically exist per retrieved definitions; AREA and ASSIGNABLE_AREA are both m² (consistent units); room-level fan-out is absorbed by SUM per building-period. Semantic-network: decision guides explicitly route current classification filters to FCLT_BUILDING and per-period assignable area to FCLT_BUILDING_HIST; hint join keys match documented relationships. Business: identical three-table pattern in 4+ gold metrics; Stata=32 exclusion precedent dw_1888; windowed running-sum precedent dw_3280/dw_126.\n\n**6d.** Alternative: filter on hist-table BUILDING_TYPE/SITE/OWNERSHIP instead of current — rejected because the hint anchors those filters to FCLT_BUILDING and the decision guide prefers the current snapshot for \"academic buildings at MIT\" phrasing.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_759572235c0f41cb847cdceb",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"SELECT\\n    t.BUILDING_NAME,\\n    t.FISCAL_PERIOD,\\n    t.total_room_area,\\n    SUM(t.ASSIGNABLE_AREA) OVER (\\n        PARTITION BY t.CAMPUS_SECTOR\\n        ORDER BY t.FISCAL_PERIOD, t.BUILDING_NAME\\n    ) AS running_sum_assignable_area,\\n    t.EXT_GROSS_AREA\\nFROM (\\n    SELECT\\n        b.BUILDING_NAME,\\n        b.CAMPUS_SECTOR,\\n        b.EXT_GROSS_AREA,\\n        h.FISCAL_PERIOD,\\n        h.ASSIGNABLE_AREA,\\n        SUM(r.AREA) AS total_room_area\\n    FROM FCLT_BUILDING b\\n    JOIN FCLT_BUILDING_HIST h\\n        ON b.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = h.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY\\n    JOIN FCLT_ROOMS r\\n        ON h.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = r.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY\\n    WHERE b.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC'\\n      AND b.OWNERSHIP_TYPE = 'OWNED'\\n      AND b.SITE = 'MIT'\\n      AND r.MAJOR_USE_DESC IN ('RESIDENT', 'LABS')\\n      AND b.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> '32'\\n    GROUP BY\\n        b.BUILDING_NAME,\\n        b.CAMPUS_SECTOR,\\n        b.EXT_GROSS_AREA,\\n        h.FISCAL_PERIOD,\\n        h.ASSIGNABLE_AREA\\n    HAVING SUM(r.AREA) > 1000\\n) t\\nORDER BY t.FISCAL_PERIOD, t.BUILDING_NAME\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
